irst defers and the\n902:async fn append_notify_superseded_when_entry_truly_lost() {\n1046:/// Notify-path (`TaggedProposal` / `Assigned`) backpressure is covered by\n1137:/// Regression test: `TaggedProposal` / `Assigned` used to go out via\n1145:/// drain so accepting that proposal must enqueue an `Assigned` against a\n1176:    // --- Phase 2: Assigned on a full leader outgoing channel ---\n1187:        .expect(\"leader stalled enqueueing Assigned on a full outgoing channel\");\n1308:/// (`unconfirmed_local`): entries deferred by leader-side batching\n1309:/// (`batch_size > 1`) are matched to their eventual log index purely by\n1311:/// share the exact same per-node batch buffer\n1312:/// (`state_cache.batched_entries`), so if an *untracked* `append()` entry\n1313:/// is batched ahead of a still-pending tracked `append_notify()` entry, and\n1317:/// Uses a real 3-node cluster with `batch_size: 4` so the interleaving below\n1324:async fn append_notify_index_correct_when_batched_with_plain_append() {\n1345:            batch_size: 4,\n1346:            flush_batch_tick_timeout: 100,\n1379:    // A1, N1, A2, N2 -- i.e. an untracked entry landing in the batch ahead\n1381:    // mishandled. All four land in one flush since `batch_size == 4`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
