erent decided value at its assigned index before the actor drains notifiers?',importance='A false successful write acknowledgment can make callers believe a write committed when its value is absent from the decided log.',source_ids=impl+ex,participants=['origin actor and old leader','replacement leader','quorum follower'],objects=['Pending EntryId assignment','ballot-specific log slot','oneshot result'],contexts=['leader change between local acceptance and notifier drain','same configuration'],event_paths=['AppendNotify -> local append_tracked assignment -> new quorum leader decides replacement -> AcceptSync replaces origin log -> tick drain_notifiers'],activity_classes=['A7','A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['b_notify_assignment','b_notify_completion'],fact_ids=['f_notify_assignment'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b_prepare':'New authority chooses eligible history excluding the isolated old leader value.','b_accept':'Replacement is decided through the actual new write quorum.','b_recover':'Restored old leader synchronizes under the newer promise.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Superseded branch explicitly compares ballots and existing test expects it when original entry is lost.','A value may survive a ballot change, so ballot mismatch alone is not a violation oracle.'],unknowns=['Whether replacement decision can reach the origin before its next notifier drain and yield a successful result.'],trigger_rationale='drain_notifiers chooses idx<=decided before ballot invalidation. The existing superseded test refills the position only after waiting for Superseded, excluding the overlap. A bounded public-API history can decide the replacement before the first configured actor tick, resolving this concrete ordering discriminator.',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',disposition='ready_for_check',priority=3)\nclaim=dict(id=cid,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='A successful append_notify completion at a returned log index must identify the submitted entry as the decided content at that index; deciding a replacement entry at the same position under a later ballot must not supply successful completion of the original invocation.',source_ids=impl+ex,scope=dict(description='Locally assigned append_notify across a same-configuration leader change, with original entry excluded from the new quorum history and a different entry decided at the assigned position.',assumptions=['Unique distinguishable values and one outstanding notify operation.','Default MemoryStorage and no snapshots.','Real executor timer; operations and transport can complete before the next actor tick.'],excluded=['Timeout accuracy','Batched assignment','Remote Assigned reply identity','Disk crash recovery']),pending=[],grounding=gr('append_notify promises to await its entry decision; Superseded documentation says the actor stops rather than confirms a potentially lost entry. Its heuristic caveat permits false negative uncertainty, not a successful acknowledgment of different decided content. The existing superseded test explicitly demonstrates a replacement at the same index.'))\nbinding=dict(id=bid,material_id='s_runtime_drain',symbol='drain_notifiers',start_line=201,end_line=222,description='Chooses successful position-based completion before ballot supersession.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=cid,source_ids=impl+ex,rationale='Consumes assignment context to complete the caller operation.')])\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Investigate a different identity-preservation responsibility at the runtime decision consumer.',map_path='runtime_map.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=[binding])\nplan=dict(description='Prepare a three-node group under node 1; move node 1 into the runtime actor. Isolate its generated acceptance of notify value 42. Nodes 2 and 3 acquire a newer ballot and decide 99 at slot 1. Restore node 1 through actual preparation and synchronization before its first five-second tick, then observe its pending result and decided content.',claim_id=cid,binding_ids=[bid],harness=dict(execution_package='./omnipaxos_runtime',kind='rust_test',source='',files={},description='Mixed public-API actor/core driver with conforming Tokio AsyncRuntime adapter. Real five-second timer permits construction before notifier polling.',semantic_changes=['No target modifications. Custom AsyncRuntime uses tokio::spawn and tokio::time::sleep without altered time.','Other two replicas are driven synchronously through core APIs. An unused node-1 placeholder preserves vector indexing and never receives protocol traffic.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='admitted',event='notify_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='isolated_accept_messages',value=2)]),dict(alias='replacement',event='replacement_observed',conditions=[dict(field='operation',reference='admitted.operation'),dict(field='decided',value=1),dict(field='replacement',value=99)])],legality=gr('Initial public prepare completes before actor ownership transfer. Admission is witnessed by two generated AcceptDecide messages for 42; neither reaches peers. The new quorum excludes the old leader, then a restored PrepareReq/Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync exchange replaces its log with actual decided 99. Incoming queue dispatch precedes following read commands because run prioritizes incoming over commands; read returns actual decided state. Setup asserts completion before the first five-second timer, but does not require any principal result. Timeout bounds missing completion rather than claiming a deadline violation. Event channel capacity exceeds generated state changes and needs no independent consumer for this finite run.')),\nmonitors=[dict(id='monitor_notify_identity',checker_id='check_notify_identity',event='notify_result',binding_ids=[bid],admission_alias='admitted',grounding=gr('One operation identity is declared before the result. The observed replacement prerequisite independently establishes a different decided entry before the notifier tick. For an actual successful result, read_decided_suffix returns the content at returned index minus one, following the runtime index convention demonstrated by the existing test.'))],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='check_notify_identity',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='completed',value=True),antecedent=dict(field='success',value=True),assertion=dict(field='content_at_index',reference='admitted.proposed'),identity_fields=['case','operation'],description='If the notify call succeeds, its returned index must contain its submitted value; observed non-success is bounded holds and does not prove universal notifier correctness.')],uncertainties=['First runtime-package compilation is not yet prepared; build failure is not protocol evidence.','One schedule tests the local unbatched assignment path; remote assignment and batching are separate contexts.'])\njson.dump(plan,open('notify_plan.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='check',rationale='Test a sourced identity-check ordering gap while retaining the confirmed independent snapshot finding.',sources=sources,candidate=candidate,plan_path='notify_plan.json',harness_path='notify_overlap.rs',files={},feedback=dict(ref_ids=['4c1e4585ab8748119316ce21b39868e9','989cd3774fd64cc7a64dbf62dd088787','b_sync','s_sync','s_memory','s_runtime_drain','s_superseded_test'],answered='The controller now confirms the snapshot-content violation with no open issues; the related map replaces its answered boundary unknown with the sourced conditional reconstruction behavior. New runtime reading identifies a different consumer: notifier success uses decided position before ballot supersession, while the existing lost-entry test waits for Superseded before deciding a replacement.',remaining=['Execute and review the independently fixed runtime overlap check.','Runtime subscriber cursor and buffered StopSign continuation remain separate leads.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The next discriminator is actual successful completion of a replaced value, not merely a changed ballot.'))\njson.dump(s,open('notify_submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['notify_submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\npython3 build_notify.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
